/-!
# The slice's base change, read over an affine chart of the arrow scheme

Let `t : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes, let `V` be an affine open of `Y`, let `b` be a section
over `V`, and let `U` be an affine open of `X` carried by `t` into `V`. The *slice* cut out of
`V` by `b` is the closed subscheme `Spec(Γ(Y, V) ⧸ (b))`, mapping to `Y` by

```
gL : Spec(Γ(Y, V) ⧸ (b)) ⟶ Spec Γ(Y, V) ⟶ Y,
```

the second arrow being the open immersion `IsAffineOpen.fromSpec`. This file computes the second
projection of the base change of `gL` along `t`, on sections over `U`: the ring map

```
Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(Spec(Γ(Y, V) ⧸ (b)) ×_Y X, pr₂⁻¹U)
```

is surjective with kernel the ideal generated by the image `t(b)` of the parameter. In other
words the base change is cut out of `U` by the single element `t(b)`.

This is the step clause (4) of Stacks 0461 turns on, and the one the repository lacked. There
`t` is the target map of a groupoid scheme, `V = Spec(A)` an affine chart of the object scheme
around `u`, `U = Spec(B)` an affine chart of the arrow scheme around the identity arrow `e(u)`,
and the conclusion is the pair of hypotheses that
`AlgebraicGeometry.quotientStalkEquivStalkOfSurjectiveApp` asks for — surjectivity of the map on
sections, and the identification of its kernel. Composing the two computes the local ring of
`U' ×_{g,U,t} R` at `(u', e(u))` as `𝒪_{R, e(u)} ⧸ (t b)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isPullback_quotientMk_appLE`: **the missing step.** The base change
  of the slice along `t`, over the affine chart `U`, is the slice of `U` cut out by the image
  ideal. This is where the factorisation of `gL` through an open immersion is used.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan`: the map on sections of
  the second projection is surjective with kernel `(t b)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_slice`: the same
  statement for the target map of a groupoid scheme, which is the form Stacks 0461 uses.

Two intermediate results are stated separately because they are about an arbitrary morphism and
are reusable:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_fromSpec`: if the base change of
  `gL : Z ⟶ Y` along `t` is affine over an affine chart `U` of `X`, then the preimage of `U` in
  the base change is an affine open.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isIso_app_of_isPullback_fromSpec`: under the same hypothesis the map
  on sections over `U` of the second projection *is* the given ring map, up to an isomorphism of
  its target. This is how a statement about a fibre product of schemes becomes a statement about
  a ring map.

## Implementation notes

The proof has three independent parts.

*The geometry of the slice.* Because `gL` factors as `q ≫ j` with `j = hV.fromSpec` an open
immersion, hence a monomorphism, a pullback square over `Spec Γ(Y, V)` remains one over `Y`:
that is `CategoryTheory.IsPullback.comp_mono`. The square over `Spec Γ(Y, V)` is the affine one,
`AlgebraicGeometry.quotientBaseChangeIso`, and the other leg of the cospan becomes
`hU.fromSpec ≫ t` by `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec`. Note that `U` is
only assumed to be *contained* in `t⁻¹V`, not equal to it, so the square
`Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ Spec Γ(Y, V)`, `X ⟶ Y` is **not** a pullback and the two squares cannot simply
be pasted; the monomorphism is what carries the identification across.

*Recognising the preimage chart.* The preimage of `U` under the second projection is an affine
open, but this is not available in advance — it is read off the identification itself, by
comparing the two pullback squares of the same cospan with
`CategoryTheory.IsPullback.isoIsPullback`. So the comparison is made twice: once with the
preimage presented as an open subscheme, which yields its affineness, and once with it presented
as `Spec` of its sections, which yields the ring map. Both times the square relating the
preimage to `U` comes from `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.isPullback`.

*Descending to rings.* An isomorphism between spectra is `Spec` of a ring isomorphism, by full
faithfulness of `Spec` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.preimage` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.map_injective`), after which the map on sections is the quotient map
composed with an isomorphism and the two conclusions are immediate.

The two conclusions are proved as separate declarations and only then paired. They are stated
over a fibre product of schemes, whose terms are large, and a single declaration proving both
exceeds the elaborator's heartbeat budget while each separately is comfortably inside it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0461](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0461)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Stacks.Groupoids

universe v u

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- **Transporting a pullback square along an isomorphism of its vertex.** -/
public theorem IsPullback.isoVertex {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {P P' X Y Z : C} {fst : P ⟶ X}
    {snd : P ⟶ Y} {f : X ⟶ Z} {g : Y ⟶ Z} (h : IsPullback fst snd f g) (e : P' ≅ P) :
    IsPullback (e.hom ≫ fst) (e.hom ≫ snd) f g :=
  h.of_iso e.symm (Iso.refl X) (Iso.refl Y) (Iso.refl Z) (by simp) (by simp) (by simp) (by simp)

end CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.quotientBaseChangeIso` for a morphism of `CommRingCat` rather than for an
algebra structure: the base change of `Spec(R/I) ⟶ Spec R` along `Spec ψ` is `Spec(S/ψ(I)S)`,
compatibly with the projection to `Spec S`.

The algebra structure the affine statement is indexed by is the one `ψ` defines, so this is a
restatement; it is made because the consumers below have a ring map to hand and not an algebra
instance, and introducing the instance inside their proofs puts `algebraMap` into every
subsequent goal. -/
public lemma exists_quotientBaseChangeIso_hom {R S : CommRingCat.{u}} (ψ : R ⟶ S)
    (I : Ideal ↥R) :
    ∃ e : pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) (Spec.map ψ) ≅
      Spec (CommRingCat.of (↥S ⧸ I.map ψ.hom)),
      e.hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map ψ.hom))) =
        pullback.snd (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) (Spec.map ψ) := by
  let _alg := ψ.hom.toAlgebra
  exact ⟨quotientBaseChangeIso I, quotientBaseChangeIso_hom_snd I⟩

/-- **The base change of a slice along a morphism, over an affine chart of the source.** Let
`t : X ⟶ Y`, let `V` be an affine open of `Y`, let `U` be an affine open of `X` with
`U ≤ t⁻¹V`, and let `I` be an ideal of `Γ(Y, V)`. Then the base change along `t` of the slice
`Spec(Γ(Y, V) ⧸ I) ⟶ Y` is the slice `Spec(Γ(X, U) ⧸ t(I)) ⟶ Spec Γ(X, U)`, over the chart
`Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ X` of the source.

**This is the step clause (4) of Stacks 0461 needs and the repository lacked:** a fibre product
along a morphism which factors through an open immersion. The affine case, with `Y` replaced by
`Spec Γ(Y, V)`, is `AlgebraicGeometry.quotientBaseChangeIso`; what the factorisation buys is
that the open immersion `hV.fromSpec` is a monomorphism, so by
`CategoryTheory.IsPullback.comp_mono` the affine square stays a pullback after both legs of its
cospan are composed with it. The hypothesis `U ≤ t⁻¹V` is an inequality and not an equality, so
the square comparing the two charts is itself not a pullback and the two cannot be pasted. -/
public lemma exists_isPullback_quotientMk_appLE {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (t : X ⟶ Y) {V : Y.Opens}
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hUV : U ≤ t ⁻¹ᵁ V)
    (I : Ideal ↥Γ(Y, V)) :
    ∃ c, IsPullback
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (t.appLE V U hUV).hom)))) c
      (hU.fromSpec ≫ t)
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) ≫ hV.fromSpec) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_quotientBaseChangeIso_hom (t.appLE V U hUV) I
  refine ⟨e.inv ≫ pullback.fst _ _, ?_⟩
  have h1 := ((IsPullback.of_hasPullback
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
    (Spec.map (t.appLE V U hUV))).comp_mono hV.fromSpec).flip
  rw [hV.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec t hU hUV] at h1
  have h2 := h1.isoVertex e.symm
  rwa [show (e.symm.hom ≫ pullback.snd
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) (Spec.map (t.appLE V U hUV))) =
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (t.appLE V U hUV).hom))) from by
      rw [Iso.symm_hom, ← he, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc]] at h2

section Chart

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (t : X ⟶ Y) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
  (gL : Z ⟶ Y) {S : CommRingCat.{u}} {ρ : Γ(X, U) ⟶ S} {c : Spec S ⟶ Z}

include hU in
/-- **The preimage of an affine chart in an affine base change is an affine open.** If the base
change of `gL : Z ⟶ Y` along `t : X ⟶ Y` restricts over an affine open `U` of `X` to
`Spec ρ : Spec S ⟶ Spec Γ(X, U)`, then the preimage of `U` under the second projection is an
affine open of the fibre product.

Both the preimage, presented as an open subscheme, and `Spec S` are pullbacks of the same
cospan, so they are isomorphic. The square exhibiting the preimage as such a pullback is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.isPullback` applied to the two open immersions
`hU.fromSpec` and the inclusion of the preimage, pasted onto the fibre square itself. -/
public lemma isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_fromSpec
    (hB : IsPullback (Spec.map ρ) c (hU.fromSpec ≫ t) gL) :
    IsAffineOpen (pullback.snd gL t ⁻¹ᵁ U) := by
  have hbase : IsPullback (pullback.snd gL t) (pullback.fst gL t) t gL :=
    (IsPullback.of_hasPullback _ _).flip
  have hsq : IsPullback (pullback.snd gL t ∣_ U ≫ hU.isoSpec.hom)
      (pullback.snd gL t ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι hU.fromSpec (pullback.snd gL t) := by
    refine IsOpenImmersion.isPullback _ _ _ _ ?_ ?_
    · rw [Category.assoc, hU.isoSpec_hom_fromSpec, morphismRestrict_ι]
    · rw [hU.opensRange_fromSpec, Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
  exact IsAffine.of_isIso ((hsq.paste_vert hbase).isoIsPullback _ _ hB).hom

include hU in
/-- **Reading the map on sections off a fibre square.** If the base change of `gL : Z ⟶ Y` along
`t : X ⟶ Y` restricts over an affine open `U` of `X` to `Spec ρ : Spec S ⟶ Spec Γ(X, U)`, then
the map on sections over `U` of the second projection is `ρ` followed by an isomorphism.

This is what turns a statement about a fibre product of schemes into a statement about a ring
map. The preimage chart being affine, the map on sections over `U` is itself a chart of the
second projection, by `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec`; comparing the two
pullback squares gives an isomorphism of spectra over `Spec Γ(X, U)`, and `Spec` is fully
faithful. -/
public lemma exists_isIso_app_of_isPullback_fromSpec
    (hB : IsPullback (Spec.map ρ) c (hU.fromSpec ≫ t) gL)
    (hW : IsAffineOpen (pullback.snd gL t ⁻¹ᵁ U)) :
    ∃ α : S ⟶ Γ(pullback gL t, pullback.snd gL t ⁻¹ᵁ U), IsIso α ∧
      (pullback.snd gL t).app U = ρ ≫ α := by
  have hbase : IsPullback (pullback.snd gL t) (pullback.fst gL t) t gL :=
    (IsPullback.of_hasPullback _ _).flip
  have hsq : IsPullback (Spec.map ((pullback.snd gL t).app U)) hW.fromSpec hU.fromSpec
      (pullback.snd gL t) := by
    refine IsOpenImmersion.isPullback _ _ _ _ ?_ ?_
    · rw [← Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app]
      exact (hU.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec (pullback.snd gL t) hW le_rfl).symm
    · rw [hU.opensRange_fromSpec, hW.opensRange_fromSpec]
  have hp := hsq.paste_vert hbase
  have hfst := hp.isoIsPullback_hom_fst _ _ hB
  set e := hp.isoIsPullback _ _ hB with hedef
  refine ⟨Spec.preimage e.hom, ⟨Spec.preimage e.inv, ?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · exact Spec.map_injective (by
      rw [Spec.map_comp, Spec.map_preimage, Spec.map_preimage, Spec.map_id, e.inv_hom_id])
  · exact Spec.map_injective (by
      rw [Spec.map_comp, Spec.map_preimage, Spec.map_preimage, Spec.map_id, e.hom_inv_id])
  · exact Spec.map_injective (by rw [Spec.map_comp, Spec.map_preimage, hfst])

end Chart

/-- A ring map which factors as the quotient by an ideal followed by an isomorphism is surjective
with that ideal as kernel. -/
public lemma surjective_and_ker_of_eq_quotientMk_comp {R T : CommRingCat.{u}} {J : Ideal ↥R}
    (f : R ⟶ T) (α : CommRingCat.of (↥R ⧸ J) ⟶ T) (hα : IsIso α)
    (hf : f = CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) ≫ α) :
    Function.Surjective f.hom ∧ RingHom.ker f.hom = J := by
  subst hf
  have hbij : Function.Bijective α.hom := ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso α
  rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
  refine ⟨by rw [RingHom.coe_comp]; exact hbij.2.comp Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective, ?_⟩
  rw [← RingHom.comap_ker, (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot α.hom).mp hbij.1,
    ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, Ideal.mk_ker]

section Keystone

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (t : X ⟶ Y) {V : Y.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) {U : X.Opens}
  (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hUV : U ≤ t ⁻¹ᵁ V) (b : Γ(Y, V))

include hU hUV in
/-- The map on sections over `U` of the second projection of the base change of the slice cut out
by `b` is surjective. -/
public lemma surjective_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan :
    Function.Surjective ((pullback.snd
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ hV.fromSpec)
      t).app U).hom := by
  obtain ⟨c, hB⟩ := exists_isPullback_quotientMk_appLE t hV hU hUV (Ideal.span {b})
  obtain ⟨α, hα, happ⟩ := exists_isIso_app_of_isPullback_fromSpec t hU _ hB
    (isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_fromSpec t hU _ hB)
  exact (surjective_and_ker_of_eq_quotientMk_comp _ α hα happ).1

include hU in
/-- The map on sections over `U` of the second projection of the base change of the slice cut out
by `b` has kernel generated by the image `t(b)` of the parameter. -/
public lemma ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan :
    RingHom.ker ((pullback.snd
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ hV.fromSpec)
      t).app U).hom = Ideal.span {t.appLE V U hUV b} := by
  obtain ⟨c, hB⟩ := exists_isPullback_quotientMk_appLE t hV hU hUV (Ideal.span {b})
  obtain ⟨α, hα, happ⟩ := exists_isIso_app_of_isPullback_fromSpec t hU _ hB
    (isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_fromSpec t hU _ hB)
  refine ((surjective_and_ker_of_eq_quotientMk_comp _ α hα happ).2).trans ?_
  rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

include hU in
/-- **The base change of a slice is cut out by the image of the parameter.** Let `t : X ⟶ Y`, let
`V` be an affine open of `Y`, let `b` be a section over `V`, and let `U` be an affine open of `X`
carried by `t` into `V`. Then the second projection of the base change along `t` of the slice
`Spec(Γ(Y, V) ⧸ (b)) ⟶ Y` has, on sections over `U`, a surjective map of rings whose kernel is
generated by the image `t(b)` of the parameter.

These are exactly the two hypotheses of
`AlgebraicGeometry.quotientStalkEquivStalkOfSurjectiveApp`, so together with that identification
this computes the local ring of the base change at a point over `U` as `𝒪_{X, x} ⧸ (t b)`. -/
public theorem surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan :
    Function.Surjective ((pullback.snd
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ hV.fromSpec)
          t).app U).hom ∧
      RingHom.ker ((pullback.snd
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ hV.fromSpec)
          t).app U).hom = Ideal.span {t.appLE V U hUV b} :=
  ⟨surjective_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan t hV hU hUV b,
    ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan t hV hU hUV b⟩

include hU hUV in
/-- The preimage of the affine chart `U` in the base change of the slice is an affine open. -/
public lemma isAffineOpen_preimage_pullback_snd_quotientSpan :
    IsAffineOpen (pullback.snd
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ hV.fromSpec)
      t ⁻¹ᵁ U) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hB⟩ := exists_isPullback_quotientMk_appLE t hV hU hUV (Ideal.span {b})
  exact isAffineOpen_preimage_of_isPullback_fromSpec t hU _ hB

end Keystone

section Stalk

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (t : X ⟶ Y) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
  (gL : Z ⟶ Y) (hW : IsAffineOpen (pullback.snd gL t ⁻¹ᵁ U))
  (hsurj : Function.Surjective ((pullback.snd gL t).app U).hom) {w : Γ(X, U)}
  (hker : RingHom.ker ((pullback.snd gL t).app U).hom = Ideal.span {w})
  {z : ↥(pullback gL t)} (hz : pullback.snd gL t z ∈ U)

include hU hW hsurj hker in
/-- **The local ring of a base change cut out by one section.** Let `gL : Z ⟶ Y` be a morphism
whose base change along `t : X ⟶ Y` is, over an affine chart `U` of `X` with affine preimage,
cut out by a single section `w` of `Γ(X, U)`. Then at a point `z` of the fibre product lying
over `U` the local ring of the fibre product is the local ring of `X` at the image of `z` modulo
the germ of `w`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.quotientStalkEquivStalkOfSurjectiveApp` with `Ideal.map_span` used to
turn the extension of the kernel into the ideal generated by one germ. Fed with the two
conclusions of `AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan` — which are
exactly its surjectivity and kernel hypotheses, with `w = t(b)` — it computes the local ring of
the base change of a slice; for the target map of a groupoid scheme that is the identification
`𝒪_{U' ×_{g,U,t} R, (u', e(u))} = 𝒪_{R, e(u)} ⧸ (t b)` on which clause (4) of Stacks 0461
rests. -/
public noncomputable def quotientStalkEquivStalkPullbackSndOfSpan :
    (X.presheaf.stalk (pullback.snd gL t z) ⧸
        Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U (pullback.snd gL t z) hz).hom w}) ≃+*
      (pullback gL t).presheaf.stalk z :=
  (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (by rw [hker, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton])).trans
    (quotientStalkEquivStalkOfSurjectiveApp _ hU hW hsurj hz)

include hU hW hsurj hker in
/-- The identification of `quotientStalkEquivStalkPullbackSndOfSpan` carries the class of the
germ of a section over `U` to the germ of its image in the fibre product. This pins it down, the
germs of sections over an affine open generating the local ring. -/
public theorem quotientStalkEquivStalkPullbackSndOfSpan_mk_germ (c : Γ(X, U)) :
    quotientStalkEquivStalkPullbackSndOfSpan t hU gL hW hsurj hker hz
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X.presheaf.germ U (pullback.snd gL t z) hz c)) =
      (pullback gL t).presheaf.germ (pullback.snd gL t ⁻¹ᵁ U) z hz
        (((pullback.snd gL t).app U) c) := by
  rw [quotientStalkEquivStalkPullbackSndOfSpan, RingEquiv.trans_apply, Ideal.quotEquivOfEq_mk]
  exact quotientStalkEquivStalkOfSurjectiveApp_mk_germ _ hU hW hsurj hz c

end Stalk

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme

/-- **The slice's base change, read over an affine chart of the arrow scheme.** Let `A` be an
affine open of the object scheme of a groupoid scheme, let `B` be an affine open of the arrow
scheme carried into `A` by the target map, and let `b` be a section over `A`. Write `gL` for the
slice `Spec(Γ(U, A) ⧸ (b)) ⟶ U`. Then the map on sections over `B` of the second projection of
`gL ×_U R` is surjective with kernel generated by `t(b)`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan` for the target map
of a groupoid scheme, which is the form Stacks 0461 clause (4) uses: the two conclusions are the
two hypotheses of `AlgebraicGeometry.quotientStalkEquivStalkOfSurjectiveApp`, so together with
that identification they compute the local ring of `U' ×_{g,U,t} R` at `(u', e(u))` as
`𝒪_{R, e(u)} ⧸ (t b)`. -/
public theorem surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_slice {S : Scheme.{u}} (G : GroupoidScheme S)
    (A : G.objects.left.affineOpens) (B : G.arrows.left.affineOpens)
    (hBA : B.1 ≤ G.target.left ⁻¹ᵁ A.1) (b : Γ(G.objects.left, A.1)) :
    Function.Surjective ((pullback.snd
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ A.2.fromSpec)
          G.target.left).app B.1).hom ∧
      RingHom.ker ((pullback.snd
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {b}))) ≫ A.2.fromSpec)
          G.target.left).app B.1).hom =
        Ideal.span {G.target.left.appLE A.1 B.1 hBA b} :=
  surjective_and_ker_app_pullback_snd_quotientSpan G.target.left A.2 B.2 hBA b

end AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme

end
